.SH NAME
omorfos \- A lightweight Wayland compositor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\fBomorfos [\-\-held]\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Chosen at the login screen, omorfos becomes omorfos\-hold, which starts the compositor beside it and starts it again if it ends, with the programs that were open still open.
.PP
The configuration is read from $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/omorfos/ (usually ~/.config/omorfos/), each file with a page of its own: config.yaml in omorfos\-config(5), keys.yaml in omorfos\-keys(5), rules.yaml in omorfos\-rules(5), menu.yaml in omorfos\-menu(5) and theme.css in omorfos\-theme(5). It is read again when it changes, and a mistake in it never breaks the session: \fBomorfosctl config check\fR says what is wrong.
.PP
What the session has to say is kept in ~/.local/state/omorfos/session.log, and what the login before said in session.log.old.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-held\fR
Take the socket from omorfos\-hold, which started it: only omorfos\-hold runs omorfos so
.TP
\fB\-h, \-\-help\fR
Print this help
.TP
\fB\-V, \-\-version\fR
Print the version
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
\fBomorfosctl\fR(1), \fBomorfos\-config\fR(5), \fBomorfos\-keys\fR(5), \fBomorfos\-rules\fR(5), \fBomorfos\-menu\fR(5), \fBomorfos\-theme\fR(5)
